---
import "../components/doze/appdraw.css";
import FirstStack from "../components/doze/FirstStack.astro";
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
---
<Page title="Download" theme="dark" current="download">
<div class="dl dl-root">
  <div>
  <section class="dl-wrap dl-s1">
    <span class="dl-eyebrow">Download</span>
    <h1 class="dl-h1 dl-s2">Get doze. Keep your fans quiet.</h1>
    <p class="dl-lede">doze is an app first: one window for every stack on your machine, with the command line inside it. Free, Apache-2.0, no account. We guessed your machine from your browser; the others are right beside it.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="dl-wrap dl-s3">
    <div class="dl-hero">
      <div class="dl-mac" aria-labelledby="dl-mac-title">
        <div class="dl-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="dl-s4">
          <img class="dl-tile" src="/brand/doze.svg" alt="">
          <div class="dl-s5">
            <span class="dl-chip dl-chip-good dl-s6">Looks like your Mac</span>
            <h2 id="dl-mac-title" class="dl-h3 dl-s7">Download doze for Mac</h2>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="dl-p dl-s8">Doze.app for Apple silicon: the window, the bat in your menu bar, and <code class="dl-ic-code">doze</code> on your PATH. Quit the app and your stacks keep running. <a class="dl-inl" href="#first-launch">What happens when you open it ↓</a></p>
        <div class="dl-stack dl-s9">
          <a class="dl-btn dl-lamp" href="https://github.com/doze-dev/doze/releases/latest">
            <svg class="dl-ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg>
            Download Doze-0.2.0.dmg
          </a>
          <div class="dl-facts">
            <span>Version <b class="dl-s10">0.2</b> · [0.2 release date]</span>
            <span>[MB]</span>
            <span>Apple silicon</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="dl-s11">
          <span class="dl-small dl-dim">Or with Homebrew</span>
          <div class="dl-cmd"><code><span class="dl-pr">$ </span>brew install --cask doze-dev/tap/doze</code><button data-copy="brew install --cask doze-dev/tap/doze" class="dl-copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy: brew install --cask doze-dev/tap/doze">Copy</button></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dl-gets dl-s12" aria-label="In the app">
          <div><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#8BE39B" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Every stack in one Library, with a switch each</span></div>
          <div><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#8BE39B" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>Tiles, List or Map: see what's awake</span></div>
          <div><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#8BE39B" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12l5 5 9-10"/></svg><span>⌘K across every stack</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dl-side">
        <div class="dl-mini" aria-labelledby="dl-linux-title">
          <h2 id="dl-linux-title" class="dl-h3">Linux</h2>
          <p class="dl-p dl-s13">x86_64 and arm64. The CLI runs on any glibc distribution. The app's packages are built and being tested on real desktops. <span class="dl-bracket">[deb and rpm at launch: confirm]</span></p>
          <div class="dl-pkgs" aria-label="Packages">
            <div class="dl-pkg"><b>App</b><span>.deb</span><span>.rpm</span></div>
            <div class="dl-pkg"><b>CLI</b><span>.tar.gz</span><span>Homebrew</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="dl-cmd dl-s14"><code><span class="dl-pr">$ </span>curl -fsSL https://doze-dev.com/install.sh | sh</code></div>
          <span class="dl-bracket">[install.sh: placeholder, not built yet]</span>
          <a class="dl-link" href="https://github.com/doze-dev/doze/releases/latest">Linux files on GitHub →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="dl-mini" aria-labelledby="dl-cli-title">
          <h2 id="dl-cli-title" class="dl-h3">Just the command line</h2>
          <p class="dl-p dl-s13">For servers, CI and terminal people. Same <code class="dl-ic-code">doze</code>, no window. Install the formula or the cask, not both: they conflict.</p>
          <div>
            <div class="dl-row"><span class="dl-small dl-dim">Homebrew</span><div class="dl-cmd"><code>brew install doze-dev/tap/doze</code><button data-copy="brew install doze-dev/tap/doze" class="dl-copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy: brew install doze-dev/tap/doze">Copy</button></div></div>
            <div class="dl-row"><span class="dl-small dl-dim">mise</span><div class="dl-cmd"><code>mise use -g ubi:doze-dev/doze</code><button data-copy="mise use -g ubi:doze-dev/doze" class="dl-copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy: mise use -g ubi:doze-dev/doze">Copy</button></div></div>
            <div class="dl-row"><span class="dl-small dl-dim">Tarball or source</span><span class="dl-small">Archives and <code class="dl-ic-code">checksums.txt</code> on <a class="dl-s15" href="https://github.com/doze-dev/doze/releases/latest">GitHub releases</a>. From source: clone the repo, then <code class="dl-ic-code">make build</code> (Go 1.27+ and bun). <code class="dl-ic-code">go install</code> is not a way in: the module carries a replace for a patched Wails.</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dl-wrap dl-fl" id="first-launch" aria-labelledby="dl-fl-title">
    <div class="dl-fl-in">
      <div class="dl-fl-say">
        <span class="dl-eyebrow">First launch</span>
        <h2 id="dl-fl-title" class="dl-h2">Open it. One password, once.</h2>
        <p class="dl-lede">The installer copies the app and puts <code class="dl-ic-code">doze</code> on your PATH, and asks nothing. The one question comes from the app, when you open it, and you can say no.</p>
        <ol class="dl-fl-steps">
          <li><b>The Library opens.</b><span>Home for every stack on this Mac. On a fresh one: three steps (open a project, bring it up, connect to it) and two ways in, drop a project folder or start empty. The bat joins your menu bar and stays when the window closes.</span></li>
          <li><b>The Machine line offers <i>Set up (one password)</i>.</b><span>It gives every service a name like <code class="dl-ic-code">gateway.larder.doze</code>, so two projects can both use 5432. It is the same setup as <code class="dl-ic-code">doze doctor --fix</code>, behind macOS’s own administrator prompt (polkit’s, on Linux), and it adds the two things <a class="dl-inl" href="#changes">listed below</a>. Skip it and everything still runs, on 127.0.0.1 with ports.</span></li>
          <li><b>Nothing starts until you flip Up.</b><span>Opening a folder never starts it. A folder with no doze.hcl shows what doze found and three ways to start, and each only writes the file.</span></li>
          <li><b>A second prompt only for your own domain.</b><span>If a stack declares <code class="dl-ic-code">domains</code>, <code class="dl-ic-code">doze trust</code> (or the stack’s banner in the app) routes them and trusts a certificate authority of this machine’s own. <a class="dl-inl" href="/doze/domains/">Your own domain, over https →</a></span></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="dl-fl-draw">
        <div class="ad dl-fl-win" role="img" aria-label="Drawing of the doze app's Library on a fresh Mac: three getting-started steps, a box to drop a project folder on, and the Machine line showing network and resolver route not set up yet, with the buttons Set up (one password) and Machine">
          <div class="ad-tb" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="ad-tab on">Home</span></div>
          <div class="ad-body" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="dl-fl-steps-d"><span class="now"><b>1</b>Open a project</span><span><b>2</b>Bring it up</span><span><b>3</b>Connect to it</span></div>
            <div class="dl-fl-drop"><b>Drop a project folder here</b><span>doze reads what is in it and says what it found before anything starts.</span><span class="ad-btn pri">Open folder… <kbd>⌘O</kbd></span></div>
            <div class="dl-fl-machine"><b>Machine</b><span><i class="ad-dot y"></i>network</span><span><i class="ad-dot y"></i>resolver route</span><span class="ad-grow"></span><span class="ad-btn pri dl-fl-pulse">Set up (one password)</span><span class="ad-btn">Machine…</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="dl-fl-note">Drawn from the app’s Library · capture pending</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dl-wrap dl-s16" aria-labelledby="dl-req-title">
    <h2 id="dl-req-title" class="dl-label dl-s17">Will it run on mine?</h2>
    <div class="dl-req">
      <div><span class="dl-s18" aria-hidden="true">●</span><b>macOS 14 Sonoma or later</b><span class="dl-small">On Apple silicon (M1 and newer).</span></div>
      <div><span class="dl-s18" aria-hidden="true">●</span><b>Linux, x86_64 and arm64</b><span class="dl-small">glibc distributions. The app needs WebKitGTK 4.1.</span></div>
      <div><span class="dl-s19" aria-hidden="true">●</span><b>No Intel Mac</b><span class="dl-small">The engines are built for Apple silicon only. Use a Linux VM.</span></div>
      <div><span class="dl-s20" aria-hidden="true">●</span><b>Windows via WSL2</b><span class="dl-small">Install the Linux CLI inside WSL2.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dl-wrap dl-s21" aria-labelledby="dl-from-title">
    <div class="dl-card dl-s22">
      <div class="dl-s23">
        <h2 id="dl-from-title" class="dl-h3">Coming from 0.1.1?</h2>
        <p class="dl-p dl-s13">Update doze first, then your modules. 0.1.1 can't read a module release's oldest-doze field, so <code class="dl-ic-code">doze modules upgrade</code> on 0.1.1 could pick a release it can't run.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="dl-from">
        <div class="dl-pre-box"><pre class="dl-pre" aria-label="Upgrade commands"><span class="dl-pr">$</span> brew upgrade doze
<span class="dl-pr">$</span> doze modules upgrade</pre><button data-copy="brew upgrade doze&#10;doze modules upgrade" class="dl-copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy the upgrade commands">Copy</button></div>
        <div class="dl-small dl-s23">
          <span>Your doze.hcl needs the new words, and doze says which line:</span>
          <span><code class="dl-ic-code">postgres "db" &#123;&#125;</code> becomes <code class="dl-ic-code">module postgres "db" &#123;&#125;</code></span>
          <span><code class="dl-ic-code">idle_timeout</code> becomes <code class="dl-ic-code">sleep</code>, and the default is 2 minutes, not 5.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dl-band">
    <div class="dl-wrap dl-sec">
      <div class="dl-two">
        <div class="dl-s24">
          <span class="dl-eyebrow">No surprises</span>
          <h2 class="dl-h2" id="changes">What doze changes on your machine.</h2>
          <p class="dl-lede dl-s25">Two at install, one at first launch if you say yes, all listed here, all undone by four commands. No kernel extension, no telemetry. The app asks GitHub for a newer doze only when you open Settings › About.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="dl-does"><span class="dl-n">1</span><div><b class="dl-s26">Copies Doze.app to Applications</b><span class="dl-p dl-s13">The window and the bat in your menu bar.</span></div></div>
          <div class="dl-does"><span class="dl-n">2</span><div><b class="dl-s26">Puts <code class="dl-ic-code">doze</code> on your PATH</b><span class="dl-p dl-s13">A link to the binary inside the app, so the CLI and the app are always the same version.</span></div></div>
          <div class="dl-does"><span class="dl-n">3</span><div><b class="dl-s26">At first launch, if you say yes: .doze names</b><span class="dl-p dl-s13">So a service gets a name like <code class="dl-ic-code">gateway.larder.doze</code> (the gateway in our example project, Larder), and two projects can both use port 5432. On a Mac it adds two things:</span>
            <ul class="dl-s27">
              <li><code class="dl-ic-code">/etc/resolver/doze</code>, which sends the .doze zone to doze's resolver and nothing else.</li>
              <li><code class="dl-ic-code">dev.doze.netd</code>, a small network daemon that gives each service a loopback address of its own.</li>
            </ul>
            <span class="dl-p dl-s13">On Linux: the <code class="dl-ic-code">doze-netd</code> systemd unit and a drop-in for your DNS manager. Only doze uses it: doze AWS and doze Kafka, run on their own, listen on 127.0.0.1 and need none of this. Skip it and everything runs on 127.0.0.1.</span>
          </div></div>
          <div class="dl-does"><span class="dl-n">+</span><div><b class="dl-s26">Only if you declare your own domain</b><span class="dl-p dl-s13"><code class="dl-ic-code">doze trust</code> makes a certificate authority for this machine. Its key stays in <code class="dl-ic-code">~/.doze/ca</code>, readable by you alone.</span></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dl-card dl-undo dl-s28">
        <div class="dl-s29">
          <h3 class="dl-h3">Take it all back</h3>
          <p class="dl-p dl-s13">Run these in order. The last one deletes every engine, every module and every project's data under <code class="dl-ic-code">~/.doze</code>, so keep it for when you mean it.</p>
          <p class="dl-small dl-s30">Still on 0.1.1? It installed none of the above:</p>
          <div class="dl-pre-box"><pre class="dl-pre" aria-label="Uninstall doze 0.1.1"><span class="dl-pr">$</span> brew uninstall doze
<span class="dl-pr">$</span> rm -rf ~/.doze</pre><button data-copy="brew uninstall doze&#10;rm -rf ~/.doze" class="dl-copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy the 0.1.1 uninstall commands">Copy</button></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dl-pre-box"><pre class="dl-pre" aria-label="Uninstall commands"><span class="dl-pr">$</span> doze dns-setup --uninstall  <span class="c"># resolver file, daemon</span>
<span class="dl-pr">$</span> doze trust --remove         <span class="c"># if you used domains</span>
<span class="dl-pr">$</span> brew uninstall --cask doze
<span class="dl-pr">$</span> rm -rf ~/.doze              <span class="c"># all data</span></pre><button data-copy="doze dns-setup --uninstall  # resolver file, daemon&#10;doze trust --remove         # if you used domains&#10;brew uninstall --cask doze&#10;rm -rf ~/.doze              # all data" class="dl-copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy the uninstall commands">Copy</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dl-wrap dl-sec" aria-labelledby="dl-verify-title">
    <div class="dl-two">
      <div class="dl-s24">
        <span class="dl-eyebrow">Trust, but check</span>
        <h2 id="dl-verify-title" class="dl-h2">Verify your download.</h2>
        <p class="dl-lede dl-s25">Every release on GitHub carries <code class="dl-ic-code dl-s31">checksums.txt</code> with the sha256 of each file. Doze.app is signed with a Developer ID and notarised by Apple, so it opens without a warning.</p>
        <p class="dl-p">Engines and modules that doze downloads later are signed too, and checked before they run.</p>
        <a class="dl-link" href="/registry/trust/">How signing works →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="dl-s24">
        <div class="dl-pre-box"><pre class="dl-pre" aria-label="Check the checksums"><span class="c"># in the folder you downloaded to</span>
<span class="dl-pr">$</span> shasum -a 256 -c checksums.txt \
    --ignore-missing
Doze-0.2.0.dmg: <span class="s">OK</span></pre><button data-copy="shasum -a 256 -c checksums.txt \&#10;    --ignore-missing" class="dl-copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy the checksum command">Copy</button></div>
        <div class="dl-pre-box"><pre class="dl-pre" aria-label="Check the app signature"><span class="dl-pr">$</span> spctl -a -vv /Applications/Doze.app
<span class="c"># accepted</span>
<span class="c"># source=Notarized Developer ID</span>
<span class="c"># origin=Developer ID Application:</span>
<span class="c">#   [team name]</span></pre><button data-copy="spctl -a -vv /Applications/Doze.app" class="dl-copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy the signature check">Copy</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dl-band">
    <div class="dl-wrap dl-sec dl-s32">
      <FirstStack id="dl-first" kicker="Then" title="Your first stack, in the app." sub="The first Up downloads the engines the stack needs, so give it a minute. After that it starts in seconds, and works offline." />
      <div class="dl-then-cli">
        <div class="dl-s33">
          <h3 class="dl-h3">From a terminal instead</h3>
          <p class="dl-p dl-s13">The same three steps. <code class="dl-ic-code">doze init</code> reads the repo the way the app does. Or borrow our example project, Larder, a made-up grocery service in Go, Python and TypeScript, and stock its shelves once.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dl-then-pres">
          <div class="dl-pre-box"><pre class="dl-pre"><span class="dl-pr">$</span> cd your-project
<span class="dl-pr">$</span> doze init
<span class="dl-pr">$</span> doze up</pre><button data-copy="cd your-project&#10;doze init&#10;doze up" class="dl-copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy the init and up commands">Copy</button></div>
          <div class="dl-pre-box"><pre class="dl-pre"><span class="dl-pr">$</span> git clone \
    https://github.com/doze-dev/doze-examples
<span class="dl-pr">$</span> cd doze-examples/larder
<span class="dl-pr">$</span> doze up
<span class="dl-pr">$</span> doze task seed-catalog</pre><button data-copy="git clone https://github.com/doze-dev/doze-examples&#10;cd doze-examples/larder&#10;doze up&#10;doze task seed-catalog" class="dl-copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy the Larder commands">Copy</button></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="dl-stack dl-s35">
        <a class="dl-btn dl-ghost" href="/examples/">Tour the Larder example</a>
        <a class="dl-btn dl-ghost" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dl-wrap dl-s36">
    <div class="dl-card dl-stack dl-s37">
      <div class="dl-s38">
        <b class="dl-s25">What's in each release</b>
        <span class="dl-p dl-s13">Newest: doze 0.2, [0.2 release date].</span>
      </div>
      <div class="dl-stack dl-s39">
        <a class="dl-link" href="/changelog/">Changelog →</a>
        <a class="dl-link" href="https://github.com/doze-dev/doze/releases">Older versions on GitHub →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  </div>

  </div>
</Page>

<style>
*{box-sizing:content-box}
button,select,input[type=button],input[type=submit],input[type=reset],input[type=search]{box-sizing:border-box}
.dl-root{line-height:normal}

.dl{font-family:var(--font-text);color:#F4ECE4;background:#140C1B;min-height:100%}
.dl a{color:#F0A24B;text-decoration:none}.dl a:hover{color:#FFC27A}
.dl :focus-visible{outline:2px solid #F0A24B;outline-offset:2px}
.dl code,.dl pre{font-variant-ligatures:none}
.dl-wrap{max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto;padding-left:32px;padding-right:32px}
.dl-sec{padding-top:96px;padding-bottom:96px}
.dl-band{background:#1A1022;border-top:1px solid #2E1F3A;border-bottom:1px solid #2E1F3A}
.dl-eyebrow{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#F0A24B}
.dl-h1{margin:0;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:800;font-size:80px;line-height:.98;letter-spacing:-0.04em;text-wrap:balance}
.dl-h2{margin:0;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:800;font-size:50px;line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-0.03em;text-wrap:balance}
.dl-h3{margin:0;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:700;font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.01em}
.dl-lede{margin:0;font-size:20px;line-height:1.55;color:#D6C8DF;max-width:44rem}
.dl-p{margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#C9BAD3}
.dl-dim{color:#9C8AAB}
.dl-small{font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;color:#C9BAD3}
.dl-ic{width:20px;height:20px;flex:none}
.dl-label{margin:0;font:600 13px var(--font-text);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#9C8AAB}
.dl-ic-code{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:14px;color:#F4ECE4;background:#120A18;border:1px solid #2E1F3A;border-radius:6px;padding:1px 6px;white-space:nowrap}
.dl .dl-btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:10px;min-height:52px;padding:0 24px;border-radius:12px;font-weight:600;font-size:16px;box-sizing:border-box}
.dl .dl-lamp{background:#F0A24B;color:#2A1534}.dl .dl-lamp:hover{background:#FFB866;color:#2A1534}
.dl .dl-ghost{border:1px solid #4A3458;color:#F4ECE4}.dl .dl-ghost:hover{border-color:#7A5E8C;color:#FFFFFF}
.dl .dl-link{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:44px;font-weight:600}
.dl-copy{flex:none;height:44px;min-width:60px;padding:0 12px;border-radius:9px;border:1px solid #4A3458;background:#2A1C36;color:#F4ECE4;font:600 13px var(--font-text);cursor:pointer}
.dl-copy:hover{border-color:#7A5E8C}
.dl-cmd{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;background:#1E1328;border:1px solid #4A3458;border-radius:12px;min-height:56px;padding:0 6px 0 16px;box-sizing:border-box}
.dl-cmd code{flex:1;min-width:0;font:15px var(--font-mono);color:#F4ECE4;white-space:pre;overflow-x:auto;padding:12px 0}
.dl-pr{color:#9C8AAB}
.dl-pre-box{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:4px;background:#120A18;border:1px solid #2E1F3A;border-radius:16px;min-width:0}
.dl-pre-box .dl-copy{margin:8px 8px 8px 0}
.dl-pre{margin:0;font:14px/1.75 var(--font-mono);color:#D6C8DF;white-space:pre;overflow-x:auto;padding:18px 22px}
.dl-pre-box .dl-pre{flex:1;min-width:0;padding-right:8px}
.dl-pre .c{color:#9C8AAB}.dl-pre .s{color:#8BE39B}
.dl-chip{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;height:28px;padding:0 11px;border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap}
.dl-chip-good{color:#8BE39B;border:1px solid #2F5A3A;background:#14251A}
.dl-chip-info{color:#9DC7FF;border:1px solid #2C3F66;background:#141B2C}
